# NovelGuard Architecture

Full detail: [docs/current_architecture.md](mdc:docs/current_architecture.md).

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Owner persona | Principle |
|-------|------|---------------|-----------|
| domain | `src/domain/` | 도미닉 | Pure rules, value objects, policies |
| application | `src/application/` | 유리 | Use cases, DTOs, ports |
| infrastructure | `src/infrastructure/` | 아다 | DB, FS, hashing; map to DTOs |
| gui | `src/gui/` | 지나 | PySide6 UI; no infra details |
| app | `src/app/` | 시몬 | Composition / wiring |
| tests | `tests/` | 테스 | unit / integration / golden |

## Dependency direction

- `domain` imports no other project layers.
- `application` depends on `domain` and `application.ports` only.
- `infrastructure` implements ports; hides external libraries.
- `gui` depends on use cases or application DTOs, not concrete infrastructure.
- `app` wires infrastructure, GUI, and use cases.

## Ports

- Ports live in `src/application/ports/`.
- Use cases depend on port protocols, not concrete classes.
- Port change → 유리; infra implementation → 아다; domain rules → 도미닉.

## Domain terms

- **FileEntry:** scanned file immutable facts (path, size, mtime, extension).
- **FilenameParseResult:** parsed title, range, tags from filename.
- **DuplicateGroupResult:** group verdict (file_ids, keeper, confidence, evidence).

## DON'T

- No I/O, UI, DB, or external API in `domain`.
- No concrete infrastructure imports in `application`.
- No business policy in `infrastructure`.
